
# ^ Line 1: what changed, in one line, under 72 characters.
#   Write it as an instruction, not a report: "Add the contact form
#   endpoint", not "Added" or "Adding". Then a blank line.
#
#   Everything below the blank line is WHY. That is the part worth
#   writing, because the diff already shows what changed but nothing
#   records what you were thinking. Include anything you would be
#   annoyed to have to work out again:
#
#     - what you tried that did not work, and why
#     - a number you measured rather than guessed
#     - a decision someone might otherwise quietly undo
#
#   Lines starting with # are ignored. Save and close to commit.
#   In nano that is Ctrl+O, Enter, then Ctrl+X.
#   To abandon the commit, delete everything above and save.
